**Definition 21.1 (independent birth blocks on raw exact A).** Use the
unchanged exact-Read raw installation A of §§2–3, with its actually
prepared unit seed and authentic context. For a pre-block term $s$,
an independent block $B$ is a nonempty finite set of distinct current
logical leaf addresses, each carrying its unique enabled $P$ or $S$.
Execute these edits as ordinary serial raw transactions in any order,
with no Tick inside. There is no batch primitive. Denote the resulting
term by $s[B]$ and the zero inclusion by $\iota_B$.

Each initial logical leaf cone comprises that position and all its
future logical descendants. Every successful edit of an unticked
extension belongs to a unique such cone. Unary material markers are
included in supports, but are not additional logical leaves.

